## Summary

Set out to speed up Helios Admin Resources' DOCUMENT tab, which loads all ~60k DOCUMENT rows with every reference included. In production it took ~13.5–14s to appear: ~3s server (redact ~1.0s, include ~1.1s, encode ~0.5s), ~0.5–1.6s download, and ~8s in the browser (measured in byre's Chrome: grid build ~2.6s, first layout ~1.8s, `setState` → `reorder()` ~1.7s).

Built (ian picked "option 1 plus the reorder fix"):
- `internal/db/policy.go`: grants that cannot read the row (`read *`, `read * (*)`, or a bare `true`) are marked `free`. `run.everyRow` tries a table's or column's free grants once per run; when they hold, `readable`/`columnReadable` skip the per-row/per-cell check and cache, so a super admin pays nothing per row or per cell. The per-cell cache map (about 1.3M entries for this query) was the bulk of redact's cost.
- `internal/db/query.go`: includes keep a `whole` set of rows already held whole (earlier includes, and answered rows when the query names no columns) and don't read-check, redact or merge them again. That covers the DOCUMENT→DOCUMENT `parent`/`source`/`terminal` includes.
- `web/admin/grid.js`: `sortBy` returns early when the sort is unchanged, so restoring URL state no longer re-appends every row.
- `docs/queryspeed.md` describes both server changes.

Measured on a production snapshot (laptop): server ~0.36–0.55s against 2.6–3.1s in prod (the laptop is ~3× faster at encoding, so expect ~1.2–1.5s in prod), with the same answer size; `setState` 1.7s → 0. The full page went to 5.4–9.6s locally against 13.5–14s in prod before.

Deliberately left out: building only the rows the tree shows (roots-only list, or lazy expand with server-side filters), which is the remaining ~4s of browser work for 60k rows of which ~6.4k show. ian declined it because the page is admin-only.

